# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

/src/generated/prisma

# Agent scratch. Grading and measurement agents write throwaway probe scripts
# (sweep specs, shift searches, transform readbacks) into the repo so they run
# against the project's own tooling and node_modules. It is working material,
# not source: the findings belong in docs/SCREEN-LEDGER.md and the fixes in the
# tree, and the scripts that produced them are regenerated every round.
# Named by convention so a running agent's files are ignored, never deleted
# out from under it, and never committed.
.g*tmp/
.agent-tmp/

# Scratch written by dispatched grading agents while they measure a screen.
# Not a deliverable: it is an agent's working directory, it is recreated per
# run, and leaving it untracked trips the repo's uncommitted-changes check
# mid-grade — when deleting it would break the grader still using it.
.grade/

# Same convention, prefix form: a dispatched grader writes probe scripts beside
# the harness it is measuring (docs/shotiq/_grader-*.mjs) rather than into a
# directory. Ignored for the same reason .grade/ is — they are an agent working
# file, they are recreated per run, and deleting them mid-grade breaks the agent
# still using them.
#
# THE PATTERN WAS `_grader-*` AND IT MISSED BY ONE CHARACTER. A grader wrote
# `docs/shotiq/_grader_tools.py` — underscore, not hyphen — which the hyphen
# form does not match, so the repo's uncommitted-changes check fired mid-grade
# on a file that must neither be committed (it is agent scratch) nor deleted
# (the agent was still running). A convention enforced by an exact-prefix glob
# only holds while every agent happens to punctuate the same way, and none of
# them were told to. `_grader*` covers both spellings and any future one.
_grader*
